[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3263292090","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/162335#issuecomment-3263292090","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/162335","id":3263292090,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87CgeK6","user":{"login":"HamidrezaAliakbari","id":59449785,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NDQ5Nzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59449785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari","html_url":"https://github.com/HamidrezaAliakbari","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T23:53:26Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T23:53:26Z","body":"I tested this case with both Colab nightly (2.9.0.dev20250906+cpu) and local build (2.8.0+cu126).\n\nUsing:\n\n`import torch, torch.nn.functional as F\n\nxq = torch._empty_affine_quantized((8, 6, 0, 7), scale=0.07663, zero_point=85, dtype=torch.quint8)\nF.interpolate(xq, size=(4, 9), mode='nearest')\n`\n\nand also with scale_factor=2.0, the calls succeed and return valid quantized outputs.\n\nThe earlier traceback (ValueError: either size or scale_factor should be defined) was expected, since calling interpolate(x) without size or scale_factor is invalid.\n\nSo at the moment I can’t reproduce a crash on quantized tensors with zero-sized dims. behavior matches float path.\n\nCould you confirm if there’s another repro case or environment where it still crashes? If not, this may be safe to close.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3263292090/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"HamidrezaAliakbari","id":59449785,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NDQ5Nzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59449785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari","html_url":"https://github.com/HamidrezaAliakbari","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidrezaAliakbari/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3263319849","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/162335#issuecomment-3263319849","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/162335","id":3263319849,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87Cgk8p","user":{"login":"cx104906","id":104093457,"node_id":"U_kgDOBjRXEQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104